---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
import { InsetText } from "@i-dot-ai-npm/component-library-solid";
---

<ToolingLayout
  title="Set up Claude Desktop"
  currentPath="/tooling/claude-desktop"
>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Set up Claude Desktop</h1>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    You can use the AI Gateway with Claude Desktop, allowing you to interact
    with Claude & third party models within your desktop environment.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Before you start, make sure you have{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
      your AI Gateway key
    </a>
    . Then, to set up Claude Desktop, you need to:
  </p>
  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#use-admin-permissions">
        Use admin permissions
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#install-claude-desktop">
        Install Claude Desktop
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      (If needed){" "}
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#add-your-key">
        Add or renew your AI Gateway key
      </a>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These steps work for most setups. If you run into issues you can't resolve,
    contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel on i.AI Slack.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="use-admin-permissions">
    Use admin permissions
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You need (temporary) admin permissions to install software on your Mac.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Select the padlock icon (<strong>Local Admin Management</strong>) on the
      top menu bar.
    </li>
    <li>
      Choose <strong>Install an app</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>Start session</strong>, and enter your laptop password.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>OK</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These permissions last for 10 minutes. Select the padlock to request more
    time.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="install-claude-desktop">
    Install Claude Desktop
  </h2>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To install Claude Desktop on your Mac, download the latest version from
      the{" "}
      <a
        class="govuk-link"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        href="https://claude.com/download"
      >
        Claude website
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Once downloaded, open the .dmg file and drag the Claude Desktop app to
      your Applications folder.
    </li>
    <li>
      The first time you open Claude Desktop, you may be prompted to sign in on
      a pre-existing account. Instead, from the top menu bar, select{" "}
      <strong>Help</strong> -> <strong>Troubleshooting</strong> ->{" "}
      <strong>Enable Developer Mode</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      A new option on the top bar will appear called <strong>Developer</strong>.
      Select it, then select <strong>Configure third-party inference</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      In the window that appears, select <strong>Connection</strong>, then
      select <strong>Gateway</strong> in the dropdown. You'll be provided a
      series of fields to fill in. Enter the following, keeping other options
      blank:
      <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Gateway Credentials</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>
          <strong>Credential Kind: </strong>
          <code>Static API key</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gateway base URL: </strong>
          <code>https://llm-gateway.i.ai.gov.uk</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gateway API Key: </strong>
          <code>[YOUR GATEWAY API KEY]</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gateway auth scheme: </strong>
          <code>bearer</code>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Models</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>
          <strong>Model Discovery: </strong>
          <p>
            Enable if you want all available models on the gateway (
            <strong>This will result in a significant amount of models</strong>)
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Model List:</strong>
          <p>
            Add specific models onto the model list. the Model ID field should
            correspond to{" "}
            <a
              class="govuk-link"
              href="https://github.com/i-dot-ai/core-llm-gateway/blob/main/backend/config/config.yml"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              config.yml
            </a>
            , using the <strong>model_name</strong> identifier
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Once configured, you can use Claude Desktop with the gateway integration.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="add-your-key">
    Add or renew your AI Gateway key
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">If you do not have an AI Gateway key:</p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Copy your AI Gateway key (
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
      how to get your key
    </a>
    ).
  </p>
</ToolingLayout>
